    "details": {
      "alignment": "Unaligned",
      "type": {
        "value": "construct",
        "subtype": "Fawful-Bot"
      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Fawful's Forces packet sheet — Hypno-Helm.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/fawfuls-forces.json</code> (entry <code>hypno-helm</code>): Tiny construct (Fawful-Bot), Unaligned; CR 2 (proficiency +2, to hit +5 with DEX); AC 14 (helmet shell), hit points 36 (8d4+16), speed 30 ft., climb 30 ft.. A GM scene kit for the Fawful's Forces article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>The helm is the same make as the one Fawful's double wore at Bowser's Castle in 1035 BF, miniaturised and given legs. The faction article lists the occupation's second verb as \"mutate\"; this is the first — a crawling helmet that hunts a head, clamps on, and starts giving orders in Fawful's voice. The Vat-Warped Thralls in the Bean Garrison folder are what a Hypno-Helm looks like a month later.</p><p>Expect it to go for the party's biggest hitter. The host's friends have three choices: knock the helm off (an action, Athletics), hit it off (attacks that miss narrowly hit the friend), or knock the friend out of the fight until the save sticks. Tearing it off hurts; leaving it on hurts more.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> controller · <strong>tier:</strong> Fawful-Bot · <strong>folder:</strong> Fawful's Furious Freaks / Machines of Fury.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/fawfuls-forces/hypno-helm.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 410004, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded cartoon character art in the style of Mario &amp; Luigi RPG concept art, bold dark outlines, flat colours, simple shading. A green dome-shaped robotic helmet with a glowing hypnotic spiral visor on the front, a brass funnel on top, a thin antenna with a red bulb, walking on four thin brass spider legs with little claws. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
