    {
      "_id": "CSAcrl4rgHSsaYZ7",
      "name": "Riding the Host",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/control/encase-creature-spider-hold.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>While attached, the helm moves with the host and has three-quarters cover from everyone but the host. An attack roll against the attached helm that misses by 4 or less hits the host instead. The helm comes off when it drops to 0 hit points or when a creature within 5 feet of the host uses an action to tear it off with a successful DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check (the host can't do this itself while charmed). When it comes off, the host takes 1d6 psychic damage as the swirl stops and is no longer charmed.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
